# nr-office-comrs-switch-word: docx (every one-shot docx call, `detect`, every docx session) is served by the Rust host.
# Compiled list: native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/route.rs RUST_HOST_FORMATS = &["docx"] (done in this task).
# Depends on nr-office-comrs-word-read and nr-office-comrs-word-edit being applied first (the docx entries of the readers and editors tables of
# src/drivers.rs): the Rust host answers every docx action only with both. xlsx and pptx stay on powershell.exe.
# Nothing was compiled (the lead builds the wave). No protocol row, no service, no SERVICE_PENDING name, no Cargo.lock change.

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/Cargo.toml (not owned by this task)
Test target, after `[[test]] name = "word_edit_live"` (or after `word_read_live` if that fragment is not applied yet):

    [[test]]
    name = "switch_word_live"
    path = "tests/switch_word_live.rs"

## 2. The composer of the transport (wherever OfficeComConfig::new is called for the daemon)
`OfficeComConfig::rust_host_program` defaults to std::env::current_exe(): in the daemon that is mixdogd, which is what
`office-com-host` needs. A composer that runs inside another binary must set `config.rust_host_program` to the mixdogd path,
because a docx call now starts `<rust_host_program> office-com-host [--session] --data-dir <dir>`.

## 3. Tests that build the transport with the shipped list (edited in this task)
tests/twin_detect.rs sets `config.rust_host_program` to target/<profile>/mixdogd.exe (or MIXDOG_TEST_MIXDOGD) because `detect` is now served by
the Rust host: `cargo build -p mixdog-cli` before running it.
